<title>BULGARIA: BULGARIA TWO-YEAR T-NOTE ISSUE 1.0 PCT SOLD.</title>
<headline>BULGARIA TWO-YEAR T-NOTE ISSUE 1.0 PCT SOLD.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgaria's Finance Ministry offer</p>
<p>of 200 million levs of two-year floater coupon T-notes was just</p>
<p>one percent sold at 82 levs per 100 levs par value, the</p>
<p>Bulgarian National Bank (BNB) said.</p>
<p>The issue was offered with no minimum acceptable price set</p>
<p>in advance by the ministry for the Friday's auction.</p>
<p>The semi-annual coupon was set equal to the BNB's central</p>
<p>interest rate (CIR) for the period to maturity. The CIR is now</p>
<p>set at 15 percent monthly or 180 percent annually.</p>
<p>One financial institution took part in the auction, the</p>
<p>BNB said.</p>
<p>The BNB did not say what the yield of the paper was.</p>
<p>Finance Ministry officials were not available for comment.</p>
<p>Details of the issue follow. Prices are in percent of par:</p>
<p> Issue number	 BG 2032796125</p>
<p> Par value	    200 mln levs</p>
<p> Bids received	  2 mln levs</p>
<p> Avg price of bids   82 pct</p>
<p> Bids approved	  2 mln levs</p>
<p> Avg accepted price  82 pct</p>
<p> Auction date	 November 8, 1996</p>
<p> Issue date	   November 14, 1996</p>
<p> Maturity date	November 12, 1998</p>
<p> Coupon payments:   May 15, 1997; November 13, 1997;</p>
<p>			  May 14, 1998; November 12, 1998</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 981 8569</p>
</text>
